From 751b9c32b4e7a109fa95e124f7ab7920cd812c59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arena-agent <arena-agent@local>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 15:41:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stop paying for a SAP setup to buy a licence
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

acquireLicense() renewed the token first, unconditionally, to guard against
Apple's 2034/2042. authenticate() begins with prepareSigner(), so that
defensive refresh cost a whole SAP setup on every click — several minutes on
the devices that have been measured.

purchaseApp() reads only the passwordToken, DSID, store front, cookies and
device identifier, all of which the account already has once it has signed in.
So purchase with those, and sign in again only once Apple actually says the
token has expired.

Downloads get the same treatment. failureType 9610 from getDownloadInfo() means
the account has no licence for that app yet, and acquiring one needs no
signature, so it happens automatically and the download is retried instead of
failing and pointing at another button.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 frontend/src/hooks/useDownloadAction.ts       |  47 ++++--
 .../tests/hooks/useDownloadAction.test.tsx    | 150 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 184 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 frontend/tests/hooks/useDownloadAction.test.tsx

